---
import Skyline from '../components/Skyline.astro';
const title = 'How we built the skyline | BitBrd';
const description = 'The living New Orleans skyline on bitbrd.com is 320 vector shapes, 3.3KB gzipped, zero JavaScript. Watch it assemble, layer by layer.';
---
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8" />
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
<title>{title}</title>
<meta name="description" content={description} />
<link rel="canonical" href="https://bitbrd.com/skyline" />
<link rel="icon" href="/favicon.png" />
<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin />
<link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Press+Start+2P&family=Inter:wght@400;500;600;700&display=swap" rel="stylesheet" />
<style>
:root{--navy:#0F3F7A;--navy-900:#082545;--navy-800:#0A1F3D;--sky:#9FD4F2;--sky-light:#CFE9F7;--ink:#0A1628;--cream:#F7FAFD;--text:#E8F2FC;--muted:#8CA3BA;--border:rgba(159,212,242,0.15)}
*{margin:0;padding:0;box-sizing:border-box}
body{font-family:'Inter',system-ui,sans-serif;background:var(--ink);color:var(--text);line-height:1.65}
.wrap{max-width:980px;margin:auto;padding:60px 24px}
.eyebrow{font-family:'Press Start 2P',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--sky);letter-spacing:0.15em;text-transform:uppercase}
h1{font-family:'Press Start 2P',monospace;font-size:clamp(1.1rem,3vw,1.7rem);color:var(--cream);margin:16px 0 14px;line-height:1.5}
.lede{color:var(--muted);max-width:62ch;margin-bottom:28px}
.stage{border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:10px;overflow:hidden;background:var(--ink)}
.statrow{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr);gap:16px;margin:30px 0}
.stat{background:var(--navy-800);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:8px;padding:18px;text-align:center}
.stat b{display:block;font-family:'Press Start 2P',monospace;font-size:1.1rem;color:#34D399;margin-bottom:8px}
.stat span{font-size:0.8rem;color:var(--muted)}
.how{margin:36px 0;color:var(--muted);max-width:68ch}
.how h2{font-family:'Press Start 2P',monospace;font-size:0.85rem;color:var(--cream);margin:26px 0 10px;line-height:1.6}
.how p{margin-bottom:12px;font-size:0.95rem}
.how b{color:var(--text)}
.btns{display:flex;gap:14px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin:4px 0 8px}
.btn{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:8px;padding:13px 22px;font-weight:600;font-size:0.9rem;border-radius:5px;border:none;cursor:pointer;text-decoration:none}
.btn-p{background:var(--sky);color:var(--navy-900)}
.btn-p:hover{background:var(--sky-light)}
.btn-g{border:1px solid rgba(159,212,242,0.35);color:var(--sky);background:transparent}
.btn-g:hover{border-color:var(--sky)}
@media(max-width:700px){.statrow{grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr)}}

/* ── assembly animation: layers arrive by paint color ── */
.stage.play :global(rect[fill="#16365C"]){animation:lyIn 0.9s ease-out 0.2s backwards}
.stage.play :global(rect[fill="#0F2A4A"]),.stage.play :global(polygon[fill="#0F2A4A"]){animation:lyIn 0.9s ease-out 1.0s backwards}
.stage.play :global(rect[fill="#091B33"]),.stage.play :global(polygon[fill="#091B33"]){animation:lyIn 0.9s ease-out 1.8s backwards}
.stage.play :global(rect[fill="#3E6B9E"]){animation:lyIn 0.9s ease-out 2.6s backwards}
.stage.play :global(.clouds),.stage.play :global(.moon){animation:lyFade 1.2s ease-out 3.3s backwards}
.stage.play :global(.lw){animation-delay:4s!important}
.stage.play :global(.lw0){animation-name:lightsA}
@keyframes lyIn{from{opacity:0;transform:translateY(14px)}to{opacity:1;transform:none}}
@keyframes lyFade{from{opacity:0}to{opacity:1}}
@media (prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){.stage.play :global(*){animation-delay:0s!important;animation-duration:0.01s!important}}
</style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="wrap">
  <span class="eyebrow">BitBrd &middot; under the hood</span>
  <h1>This skyline is 3.3 kilobytes.</h1>
  <p class="lede">The living New Orleans skyline at the bottom of our site &mdash; cathedral, Superdome, the Crescent City Connection, 92 windows blinking on their own schedules &mdash; is smaller than a single emoji image. Watch it assemble:</p>

  <div class="stage play" id="stage"><Skyline /></div>

  <div class="statrow">
    <div class="stat"><b>320</b><span>vector shapes</span></div>
    <div class="stat"><b>3.3 KB</b><span>over the wire (gzipped)</span></div>
    <div class="stat"><b>0</b><span>JavaScript, images, libraries</span></div>
    <div class="stat"><b>92</b><span>lights on independent timers</span></div>
  </div>



  <div class="btns">
    <button class="btn btn-p" id="replay">&#8635; Replay the build</button>
    <a class="btn btn-g" href="/#contact">Want a site built like this? &rarr;</a>
    <a class="btn btn-g" href="/">&larr; Back to BitBrd</a>
  </div>

  <div class="how">
    <h2>How it works, in plain English</h2>
    <p>There&rsquo;s no image file. The whole scene is <b>drawn in the page&rsquo;s own code</b> &mdash; &ldquo;rectangle here, this size, this navy&rdquo; about three hundred times. A small program we wrote generates the city: building widths and heights come from constrained randomness (no two neighbors the same height, no flat monoliths), and the landmarks &mdash; St.&nbsp;Louis Cathedral, the Superdome, the bridge &mdash; are drawn by hand from photographs.</p>
    <p>The randomness is <b>seeded</b>: the same city regenerates identically every time, which means we can edit one layer without disturbing a pixel of the rest. Every window light is its own tiny rectangle with its own on/off cycle &mdash; 7 to 26 seconds, scattered phases &mdash; so the pattern never visibly repeats.</p>
    <p>The animations run as CSS on your device&rsquo;s <b>graphics chip</b>, off the main thread &mdash; they can&rsquo;t make the page stutter. A looping video of this same scene would cost a thousand times more data.</p>
    <h2>Why it matters for your business</h2>
    <p>This is the standard your site gets. We build everything this way, right down to the decoration. Google ranks fast sites higher, and that is a big part of how our clients keep winning local search.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<script is:inline>
  document.getElementById('replay').addEventListener('click', function () {
    var st = document.getElementById('stage');
    st.classList.remove('play');
    void st.offsetWidth; // reflow to restart animations
    st.classList.add('play');
  });
</script>
</body>
</html>
